he code changes #2118 for [Issue2097](https://github.com/nunit/nunit/issues/2097), the test below still will fail, since when the `NUnitEqualityComparer` does each item comparison, the property `compareAsCollection` is still `true`,  so it will not get in the  [condition](https://github.com/nunit/nunit/blob/release/3.7/src/NUnitFramework/framework/Constraints/NUnitEqualityComparer.cs#L229), which ignoring the `IEquatable` of the element and will fail the assertion. \r\n```\r\nnamespace Nunit3TestsSamples {\r\n\t[TestFixture]\r\n\tclass TestSample1 {\r\n\r\n\t\t[Test]\r\n\t\tpublic void test() {\r\n\t\t\tvar set1 = new List<TestObject>() {\r\n\t\t\t\tnew TestObject { Value = \"test1\" },\r\n\t\t\t\tnew TestObject { Value = \"test2\" },\r\n\t\t\t\tnew TestObject { Value = \"test3\" }\r\n\t\t\t};\r\n\t\t\tvar set2 = new List<TestObject>() {\r\n\t\t\t\tnew TestObject { Value = \"test1\" },\r\n\t\t\t\tnew TestObject { Value = \"test2\" },\r\n\t\t\t\tnew TestObject { Value = \"test3\" }\r\n\t\t\t};\r\n\r\n\t\t\tCollectionAssert.AreEqual( set1, set2 );\r\n\t\t}\r\n\r\n\t\tclass TestObject : IEquatable<TestObject> {\r\n\t\t\tpublic string Value { get; set; }\r\n\r\n\t\t\tpublic bool Equals( TestObject other ) {\r\n\t\t\t\treturn Value.Equals( other.Value );\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"OmicronPersei","id":5589035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1ODkwMzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5589035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmicronPersei","html_url":"https://github.com/OmicronPersei","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmicronPersei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmicronPersei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmicronPersei/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmicronPersei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmicronPersei/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gith